A||||23||Fierochic88||Prayer for a Fellow Fiero Friend||||9||
Z||000000||Fierochic88||06-12-2001||10:32 PM||||I just recieved news from my sister which was confirmed by the local news network.  A local Fiero lover, 16 year old Dan Correll, was at the beach in New Jersey vacationing with his family.  He was digging a sand tunnel and it collapsed and buried him under there for over 20 minutes.  Upon being unburied Dan was not breathing and had no detectable heartrate.  According to the news he was revived and is in critical condition at the local hospital.  My sister heard even worse news, which I will not mention until I have a more confirmed report.  Some of you may have met Dan's folks at Carlisle.  Dan and his dad, Dennis have recently gotten into Fieros now that Dan is old enough to drive.  They both have 85 GT's and were working on them as a father-son project.  Dan couldn't come to Carlise due to another obligation but his parents came just to meet the nice Fiero people and see their lovely cars.  They approached me and introduced themselves, noticing that I too was from their town of Oley.  Apparently Dennis works with my Dad and knew of him as the man who drove a different Fiero everyday.  He came to Carlisle hoping to meet us and other local Fiero owners and to get some information on becoming involved in our club.  Dan's parents were very excited for themselves and for him and were anxiously awaiting the summer months to spend time with us Fiero folk.  Please say a prayer for Dan and his family.  I will keep everyone updated on his condition.<P>Jennifer<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||grinthock||06-12-2001||10:36 PM||||The prayers Of Myself and FieroHeather shall be heard.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jaygee79||06-12-2001||10:37 PM||||Oh that's horrible.  I'll keep him in my prayers.<P>------------------<BR>Jaime<BR>84SE red<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooheey1.jpg"> ||||reg||9
